            <ArticleTitle>Diazepam mixed micelle--comparison with diazepam in propylene glycol and midazolam.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>352-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A mixed micelle formulation of diazepam was compared with midazolam and diazepam in propylene glycol for evidence of venous intolerance following IV injection. The overall incidence of venous morbidity was 17% for diazepam mixed micelle, 26% for midazolam and 90% for diazepam in propylene glycol. Diazepam mixed micelle is suggested as a preferable alternative to the standard formulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
